/-! # Eq exposure reaches a non-level root inside a minimum eta body

Minimize over all finite stages, read every outer singleton directly, and
bypass administrative and proof-argument eta cases. The retained native eta
must itself contain a non-level cut on its original constant-headed body.

`EqRetainedSupplyHistory.consume` now carries an actually computed older
argument beneath any finite telescope of retained binders and computed
annotations. Separate insertion paths account for the removed binder.
`EqPrefixSpecializationAt.retained_telescope_selected_return` derives the
whole and inner suffix minima from the parent application predicate and recorded
run, then returns the component-only body to the chosen-chain minimum class.
Cost does not increase; at equal cost the retained-depth frame count omits the
older application. Carrying the supplied history to arbitrary nested cuts
remains open; these local preservation theorems do not close strengthening.

`interleaved_supply_selected_return` extends this return through unused actual
insertions between chosen retained binders. A typed upper map handles domains
that depend on earlier inserted variables; lower assignments need no new images.
The source annotation history can be recorded before the computed consumed
argument is known. Its outgoing contexts are filled in at consumption, and
untracked upper extras retain their exact substituted syntax. Deriving and
carrying the full supplied history through arbitrary nested cuts remains open.

The empty-local-supply cut theorems now derive history extensions from actual
non-level cuts at the whole reached spine. A short prefix opens a chosen binder;
a saturated prefix records an unused insertion and keeps the native eta argument
among the upper extras. The actual argument-free eta suffix must retain its
lambda, so both cases keep the original annotation/body paths, strict child
minimum and extended history alongside the body component-or-cut readout.
Nested supplied consumption and global continuation closure remain open.

`returning_supply_selected_return` now preserves older ancestry when consuming
a nested supplied binder beneath a positive surviving inner prefix. Outgoing
annotations receive reflexive paths at their computed values; no native guard
path is substituted. The rebuilt wrapper includes the actual waiting arguments
and rejoins the older history, while the same concrete context carries the
chosen prefix, exact upper extras and decreased selected minimum. Full nested
descent/return closure remains open.

`recognized_body_return_minimum` covers the return without surviving inner
wrappers once the body endpoint has been recognized as a typed nonproof chosen
spine in the original fresh scope. It accepts arbitrary native body computation,
recovers source equality by certificate descent and erasure reflection, restores
the whole supplied spine and derives a strict smaller suffix minimum. Producing
the recognized endpoint with the original pending images through all nested
cuts remains open; the new theorem does not establish recursive closure.

`EqPendingSupplyHistory` strengthens the wrapper history with each retained
frame's actual typed argument supply and exact pending-vector transition.
Realization preserves these records, and the actual supplied eta-origin split
constructs them in its retained branch. With an empty enclosing pending vector,
subsequent argument computation derives the chosen consumption square and
rebuilds all surviving inner supplies. The returned waiting tail remains typed
and separate; restoring it to a recursively returned whole body is still open.
Raw wrapper concatenation alone does not prove that stronger invariant.

`restore_consumed_rejoin` now restores that waiting tail when recursive body
processing supplies a positive returned history and its exact endpoint equation.
Whole-path realization and annotation reflection recover the source-domain
alignment needed by an initially argument-free retained lambda. The actual eta
step and body path reconstruct the required native return path by beta, without
substituting native computations. Source argument equalities restore the whole
application typing; pending supplies survive the reattachment and older-history
join. Constructing these returned histories at every recursive cut, with the
selected minimum and termination argument, remains open.

`counted_lambda_readout` now reads an actual chosen retained lambda suffix
without a minimum premise. It preserves the body scope and bounds the sum of
annotation, body, argument and beta-suffix primitive costs. Local consumption
splits the pending vector without requiring the enclosing tail to be empty.
`outermost` exposes the source frame and exact inner depth; outer annotation
alignment returns an identity square preserving the chosen spine and raw
wrapper. These support a direct endpoint-recognition induction, but its recursive
recognition theorem and output-depth bound remain unproved.

`compute_consumed_source` derives a typed lower returned function and its whole
waiting application from the original typed lambda application and actual body
and argument computations. It preserves the chosen supply and the exact raw
endpoint. `realized_source_rejoin` restores a returned positive history using a
reflexive native path at that realized function. Recursive state must still
retain the original whole application witnesses; individually typed supplies do
not provide them. Constructing the returned history and proving its depth bound
remain open.

`EqAnchoredPendingHistory` now retains the original source body computation and
whole application witness at every chosen frame, indexed by its actual current
endpoint. These witnesses survive full history realization, body computation
in realized contexts, outer supply restoration and joining at a matching
intermediate endpoint. `outermost` exposes the source anchor together with the
inner history. Constructing this invariant through arbitrary recursive cuts,
unused-frame consumption and the output-depth bound remain open.

`unused_counted_lambda_readout` now derives the actual unused-binder square from
the computed upper argument. `consume_unused_rejoin` realizes every surviving
anchored frame, restores raw waiting extras and rejoins older anchors at the
actual post-beta endpoint. A recognized completed prefix returns directly when
no wrappers survive. These local cases preserve lower chosen assignments and
need no target image for an unused upper argument. Their integration into the
recursive recognizer, with continuation minimality and the depth bound, remains
open.

`EqAnchoredEndpoint` now states the exact normalized output invariant, and
`EqAnchoredRecognition` names the outstanding global theorem with its typed
continuation, all-stage minimum and depth bound. The component branch, zero-cost
zero-depth base case, endpoint realization and retained-frame reconstruction are
proved. The conditional theorem `EqAnchoredRecognition.lifted_probe` shows that
the recognizer would close the original lifted Eq probe; it takes the unproved
recognizer explicitly. Consumed-case integration and the global induction remain
open, and no strict comparison with PropFront is claimed.

`EqRetainedSourceAnchor.consume_recognized` now restores the exact recognition
state after chosen-binder consumption at every returned depth. The original
whole source application supplies dependent typing; the stored body computation
and actual square supply exact post-beta erasure. Unused-binder consumption and
raw or chosen waiting tails also preserve the state. `consumed_recognition`
connects actual argument/body computations to the suffix input and proves the
lexicographic decreases from the body induction bound.
`pi_inert_lambda_recognition_readout` supplies the corresponding typed body
continuations and unrestricted body/suffix minima for an existing lambda.
Fresh eta initialization and the global depth-bounded induction remain open.

`eq_anchored_recognition` now proves the full exact recognizer by nested strong
induction on primitive cost and incoming depth. All four existing-lambda cases
use the derived original-scope body/suffix minima. Each fresh eta initializes a
depth-one state immediately, so its entire actual suffix has strictly smaller
primitive cost. `pi_inert_lifted_eq_probe_descend` therefore reads the original
lower Eq indices from any actual lifted Pi-inert carrier exposure, with no
recognizer or frontier premise. This closes the recognition obligation described
above; general semantic path coverage and the original strengthening theorem
remain separate and are not claimed here.


`pi_inert_type_probe_descend` now specializes that readout to an actual lifted
type-valued probe. Combined with the existing stage-zero converted-unit selector,
finite Pi-inert shared application implies `PropositionFront` in environments
with a closed positive empty structure; fresh-body extraction has the same
consequence. The output stage is arbitrary. This implication assumes the
application/readout law, not the recognizer, which is proved. It establishes
neither coverage nor a strictly smaller remaining obligation.

-/
